# 15. PERMISSION SECURITY

This is extremely important.

Do NOT rely only on hiding buttons or pages.

Authorization must be enforced on the backend/API/server/database layer.

For example:

A Coupon Handler should NOT be able to call an endpoint that modifies riders.

A Delivery Management account should NOT be able to modify coupons.

An Inventory Management account should NOT be able to modify customer-service cases unless explicitly permitted.

A Customer should NOT be able to access internal admin APIs.

A Store should NOT be able to access another Store's private data.

A Rider should NOT be able to access another Rider's private account or assignments unless explicitly authorized.

A role should only receive the minimum permissions necessary for its responsibilities.

