# 18. IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULES

Implement these rules clearly:

### Account creation

Public:

- Customer → Can Sign Up
- Store → Can Sign Up
- Rider → Can Sign Up

Internal:

- Admin → Created/managed according to existing Admin system
- Delivery Management → Created by Admin
- Coupon Handler → Created by Admin
- Customer Service → Created by Admin
- Inventory Management → Created by Admin

Internal roles must not have public sign-up forms.

---

### Rider management

Rider signs up normally.

Admin/authorized process verifies or manages the Rider as appropriate.

Delivery Management can manage Rider operational status and delivery-related account state.

Examples:

- Active
- Available
- Assigned
- On Delivery
- Suspended
- Inactive

Be careful not to let Delivery Management bypass higher-level account/security controls that should remain with the Admin.

---

### Merchant management

Merchant signs up.

Admin reviews merchant.

Admin approves/rejects merchant.

Only approved merchants should receive the appropriate operating permissions.

---

### Coupon management

Coupon Handler creates and manages coupons.

Customer claims eligible coupons.

System validates requirements.

Customer applies coupon during checkout.

Backend calculates/validates the discount.

Order records the applied coupon and discount.

Coupon analytics update based on actual transactions.

---

### Inventory management

Stores manage their products and relevant stock.

Inventory Management monitors all stores.

Inventory analytics calculate:

- Current stock
- Low stock
- Out of stock
- High stock
- Stock movement
- Product availability

Do not allow Inventory Management to unintentionally alter merchant-owned data unless the permission is explicitly required.

---

### Customer Service

Customers can submit complaints.

Stores can respond to complaints relevant to them.

Customer Service can monitor the entire case.

If the Store fails to respond or the customer escalates the case, Customer Service can manage the escalation process.

